.TH SDL_GetGamepadAxisFromString 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetGamepadAxisFromString \- Convert a string into
.BR SDL_GamepadAxis
enum.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gamepad.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_GamepadAxis SDL_GetGamepadAxisFromString(const char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function is called internally to translate
.BR SDL_Gamepad
mapping strings for the underlying joystick device into the consistent
.BR SDL_Gamepad
mapping\[char46] You do not normally need to call this function unless you are parsing
.BR SDL_Gamepad
mappings in your own code\[char46]
.PP
Note specially that \(dqrighttrigger\(dq and \(dqlefttrigger\(dq map to
.BR SDL_GAMEPAD_AXIS_RIGHT_TRIGGER
and
.BR SDL_GAMEPAD_AXIS_LEFT_TRIGGER ,
respectively\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I str
string representing a
.BR SDL_Gamepad
axis\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the
.BR SDL_GamepadAxis
enum corresponding to the input string, or
.BR SDL_GAMEPAD_AXIS_INVALID
if no match was found\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetGamepadStringForAxis (3)
